    {
      "cve": "CVE-2026-118599",
      "ids": [
        {
          "system_name": "SUSE CVE Page",
          "text": "https://www.suse.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-118599"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        {
          "category": "general",
          "text": "A file overwrite vulnerability exists in Epiphany when installing WebExtension packages from .xpi files.\n\nIn src/webextension/ephy-web-extension-manager.c, decompress_xpi_thread() used libarchive with archive_read_support_format_all() (and filters), so the installer did not require a real ZIP. A TAR file named *.xpi was extracted. TAR supports hard-link entry types; with Epiphany's archive_write_disk options (including ARCHIVE_EXTRACT_PERM), a crafted hard-link target can cause an attacker-chosen existing user-writable file to be truncated and overwritten with attacker-controlled content and mode bits, without a dedicated warning dialog, when the user installs or opens the crafted .xpi.\n\nThis is related to but separate from the ZIP-slip path traversal fixed as CVE-2026-77679 (#2922 / MR !2143).\n\nRequirements: the victim must install or open a malicious WebExtension (.xpi).\n\nAffected: Epiphany \u003e= 47.0 (WebExtension XPI install path).\nFixed: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/epiphany/-/merge_requests/2248 (commit 0cc9ab55 - only enable ZIP format support).\nUpstream: https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/epiphany/-/work_items/2988\nReporter acknowledgment: Fernando Munoz",
          "title": "CVE description"
        }
      ],
